.TH SDL_SetTrayEntryLabel 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_SetTrayEntryLabel \- Sets the label of an entry.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_tray.h>
.PP
.BI "void SDL_SetTrayEntryLabel(SDL_TrayEntry *entry, const char *label);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
An entry cannot change between a separator and an ordinary entry; that is, it is not possible to set a non-NULL label on an entry that has a NULL label (separators), or to set a NULL label to an entry that has a non-NULL label\[char46] The function will silently fail if that happens\[char46]

.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I entry
the entry to be updated\[char46]
.TP
.I label
the new label for the entry in UTF-8 encoding\[char46]
.SH THREAD SAFETY
This function should be called on the thread that created the tray\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

